From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Facebook integration

What the LuneOS Messaging app needs of the Facebook Messenger protocol
on top of the generic one the previous patch adds, as it was carried
before in "webOS: add a Facebook Messenger protocol" and "webOS:
Facebook typing, receipts, edits, deletes, rich sends and groups":

- the transport's webos-im-* signals for Facebook accounts (glue/login.c):
  reactions, edits and deletes for everyone sent from the app
  (gometa_actions.go), replies, locations, contact cards and mentions
  in a send (gometa_send.go), and the sent message's id and its
  delivery and read state reported back;
- group administration from the app (create, add, remove, rename,
  leave) and the members the transport asks for (gometa_groups.go);
- incoming reactions, edits and deletions put on the message they
  change, as the WhatsApp patches do, instead of a line in the chat;
- attachments through the WhatsApp protocol's download path
  (bridge.go, handle_attachment.go), with a recover() so a failed
  Facebook download cannot take the transport down;
- the protocol registered unconditionally next to WhatsApp and Matrix,
  and its E2EE store removed by the shared account-removed handler
  (glue/init.c);
- the glue tests for gometa_init.c and login.c's signal gate.

The Go files keep the generic patch's //go:build gometa line; the recipe
builds with -tags gometa.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
